            "video_1": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TKftgyQSEBQ",
            "video_2": "https://youtu.be/fw4eIVTwWpc"
          }
        },
        "f65aa26e-6f20-4e9c-a91b-0a269239be79": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "full_width_enable": true,
            "title": "Firmware",
            "text": "<p><strong>For the best performance and latest features, keep your OcuMow VBRM16 LawnMaster robot mower firmware up to date.</strong></p><p><strong>How to Install Firmware:</strong></p><p>1. Download the software file above and save it to a blank USB flash drive/memory stick. Do not change the filename. The filename should show as border - if the file has downloaded with a (1) or (2) in the filename, please re-name the file when you save it.</p><p>2. Make sure that the battery indicator is green and has sufficient charge to perform the software update. </p><p>3. Remove the safety key and turn the mower on its side on a clean, soft surface.</p><p>4. Open the USB port rubber cap (in the mower deck) to reveal the USB port.</p><p>5. Insert the safety key and long press the START/ON button for 3 seconds. Wait for the green lights to stop flashing and the mower to beep.</p><p>6. Insert the USB flash drive into the USB port. You will hear four beeps and the indicator lights will flash green. The software is now updating.</p><p>7. When the software update is complete, the mower will beep continuously, and the battery indicator light will be lit green.</p><p>8. Remove the USB flash drive and replace the rubber cap. To complete the software update, restart the machine by removing and reinserting the safety key.<br/> </p><p><strong>VBRM16 July 2023 Update 1.0:</strong></p><p>This latest firmware update improves the mowers ability to detect borders.</p>",
            "button_1_style": "black",
            "button_1_text": "Download Firmware",
            "button_1_url": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0050/9811/1010/files/border?v=1688464908",
