    "df696699-42a8-4b2a-8976-674c3e309cd21": {
      "type": "featured-accordion",
      "blocks": {
        "d7624e53-96f3-43a2-a5b4-052847d8844f": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "full_width_enable": true,
            "title": "Why are there such specific lawn border requirements?",
            "text": "<p>If the mower cannot recognise a clearly defined lawn edge, it may not stay within the lawn area. Bare earth borders which can become weedy, or flower borders with low plants can be interpreted as grass by the Optical Grass Recognition (OGR) software. For this reason, we recommend that either raised edges, a hard border of paving or gravel, or walls and fences are the best options around the lawn.</p>",
            "button_1_style": "white",
            "button_1_text": "",
            "button_1_url": "",
            "button_2_style": "link",
            "button_2_text": "",
            "button_2_url": "",
            "product_specifications": "",
            "html": "",
            "collection": "",
            "collection_products_per_page": 8,
            "products": [],
            "image_loading": "",
            "video_1": "",
            "video_2": ""
          }
        },
        "80d3ee7d-e860-4a9c-8b84-2c5508cdf136": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "full_width_enable": false,
            "title": "Can it stay on the lawn 24/7?",
            "text": "<p>Unlike traditional robots the VBRM16 OcuMow™ is designed to Drop and Mow. The mower is designed to be placed on the lawn once or twice a week and will mow for up to 4 hours on a single charge covering 100m2. The mower should be stored away in a dry place between uses.</p>",
            "button_1_style": "black",
            "button_1_text": "",
            "button_1_url": "",
            "button_2_style": "",
            "button_2_text": "",
            "button_2_url": "",
            "product_specifications": "",
